urn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The two releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were both unhealthy.\n- **Result:** After the rollback, all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** There were no open incidents before this one. INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the results afterwards. As a follow-up, it asks for the cause of the v2.3.1 / v2.3.1-rc failures to be found before anyone redeploys.", "type": "text"}]}]}